							"documentation": "Scope: an authenticated Customer follows successful UC04 main-flow input. Both theme/level and product selection independently allow GUI or voice. Error handling is omitted.\nOpenView(\"TravelProductView\") renders existing theme/grade controls. No undocumented metadata-query or display method is added, and no unrestricted customer LoadProducts(null, null) query is invented.\nBefore each RecognizeSelection, TravelProductView forms a fresh VoiceSelectionContext from selectedTheme, selectedLevel and the current productList. Logical context fields are theme, tourLevel and products; context is not an added formal parameter of SelectByVoice.\nSpeechRecognitionManager calls SpeechServiceClient.Recognize(voiceInput). The client communicates with the external speech service and returns SpeechRecognitionResult. Only a successful recognizedText is passed to VoiceSelectionInterpreter.InterpretSelection(recognizedText, context). External vendor signatures are unspecified and are not invented.\nVoiceSelectionInterpreter returns VoiceSelectionResult to SpeechRecognitionManager, which returns it to TravelProductView without changing UI state or querying Data Access. This successful-flow diagram does not apply failed, ambiguous or unsupported results.\nFor filter results, only explicitly recognized fields replace current filters. Unspecified fields are retained. The merged selectedTheme and selectedLevel supply LoadProducts(theme, level); the VoiceSelectionResult field tourLevel supplies the formal parameter level.\nFor a product result, returned productId resolves to one TravelProduct in the current productList before the UI SelectProduct(product) call. The UI then extracts that object productId for TravelManager.SelectProduct(productId). No UI SelectProduct(productId) or speech service business-selection call is invented.\nBoth GUI and voice input converge on the same TravelManager method. Product lookup, stored default configuration, option validity and unit-price calculation stay inside existing TravelManager contracts. No voice control for hotel, transport, meal, drinks or booking is added.\nThe optional ConfigureTravelProduct step groups all option changes and is drawn once. It validates a new value and returns its configuration and unit price; the old/default configuration is used if no changes are requested. currentPrice is per traveler before UC05 traveler-count/regular-customer calculations.\nAfter customer confirmation, MainView opens TravelApplicationView and TravelProductView calls ShowApplication(selectedProduct, currentConfiguration). There is no cart registration, application save, departure confirmation or SMS in UC04.\nOmitted for brevity: errors, retry/cancel branches, repeated individual option changes, session lookups, repository forwarding, default-value construction, ApplyChanges/ValidateConfiguration/CalculateUnitPrice internals and explicit theme/grade restriction branches. These successful-path rules remain part of the shown public method contracts.",
